Short-Term Ferry Ticket Demand Forecasting & Predictive Decision Support System

Abstract
This study explores the application of machine learning and time-series forecasting to predict short-term ferry ticket demand for Toronto Island Park.
By analyzing historical ticket sales and redemptions, the project demonstrates how predictive intelligence can support proactive scheduling,
staff readiness, and crowd management.

1. Introduction
Ferry operations traditionally rely on reactive responses to passenger demand.This often results in congestion, delays, and safety risks during sudden 
demand spikes. The objective of this research is to transition operations from reactive analytics to predictive intelligence, enabling ferry operators
to anticipate demand in upcoming 15-minute to 2-hour windows.
